1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:02,419
[♪ opening theme song playing]

2
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:47,965
THE PERFECT LIE

3
00:00:53,053 --> 00:00:54,638
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION

4
00:00:54,721 --> 00:00:57,975
SCENES INVOLVING CHILD ACTORS
AND ANIMALS WERE FILMED SAFELY

5
00:01:04,398 --> 00:01:06,275
[♪ dreamy music playing]

6
00:02:23,518 --> 00:02:25,103
[surgeon] <i>In the seventeenth century,</i>

7
00:02:25,187 --> 00:02:26,563
<i>the Great Plague of London</i>
<i>swept through Europe.</i>

8
00:02:27,981 --> 00:02:30,859
<i>Isaac Newton was studying</i>
<i>at Cambridge at the time.</i>

9
00:02:31,485 --> 00:02:35,155
<i>One in six people were dying,</i>
<i>so there wasn't much they could do.</i>

10
00:02:35,238 --> 00:02:37,074
The university had to shut down too.

11
00:02:39,076 --> 00:02:40,786
Newton went back home,

12
00:02:41,453 --> 00:02:43,872
and I think he ended up
taking about two years off.

13
00:02:43,955 --> 00:02:46,208
You know what he did during that time?

14
00:02:46,750 --> 00:02:47,793
Scalpel.

15
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:53,799
He came up with the law of gravity
and even invented calculus.

16
00:02:57,969 --> 00:02:59,429
This isn't the one I usually use.

17
00:03:02,516 --> 00:03:06,978
[nurse] It's from the same manufacturer,
but they changed the model.

18
00:03:07,688 --> 00:03:10,107
[surgeon] It's fine.
I'll get used to how it feels.

19
00:03:13,819 --> 00:03:15,737
- [♪ soft music plays]
- Maybe we're all just

20
00:03:15,821 --> 00:03:18,490
<i>spending our whole lives</i>
<i>struggling to keep up</i>

21
00:03:18,573 --> 00:03:21,785
<i>in a world that some geniuses</i>
<i>cobbled together by winging it.</i>

22
00:03:23,286 --> 00:03:27,374
Do you know what Newton said
about human beings?

23
00:03:28,417 --> 00:03:29,459
Cut.

24
00:03:32,671 --> 00:03:35,966
"I can calculate
the motions of the heavenly bodies,

25
00:03:36,049 --> 00:03:39,803
but not the madness of human beings."

26
00:03:41,596 --> 00:03:47,769
EPISODE 1
THE DATE

27
00:03:49,396 --> 00:03:50,522
[♪ gentle music plays]

28
00:04:14,087 --> 00:04:15,589
Breakfast's ready!

29
00:04:17,966 --> 00:04:19,885
If you don't get up,
I'm going to spray you.

30
00:04:19,968 --> 00:04:21,386
[groans]

31
00:04:27,225 --> 00:04:29,269
<i>Ten seconds before I spray you.</i>

32
00:04:30,729 --> 00:04:32,606
- <i>Nine.</i>
- Where did it go?

33
00:04:33,106 --> 00:04:35,317
- [person] <i>Eight.</i>
- Geez.

34
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:36,651
Seven.

35
00:04:37,944 --> 00:04:39,404
Six, five, four, three, two…

36
00:04:39,488 --> 00:04:41,031
Stop it. That's so childish.

37
00:04:41,114 --> 00:04:42,908
- [surgeon] Did you sleep well?
- [sighs]

38
00:04:44,034 --> 00:04:47,037
[surgeon]
Say, "Thanks for breakfast, Dad."

39
00:04:48,789 --> 00:04:50,290
Mmm.

40
00:05:01,301 --> 00:05:02,761
Your mom would be happy.

41
00:05:10,519 --> 00:05:11,853
That's my boy.

42
00:05:11,937 --> 00:05:12,938
[both chuckle]

43
00:05:14,272 --> 00:05:15,774
SOMETIMES IT RAINS IN MY HEART

44
00:05:17,526 --> 00:05:19,820
[door opens, closes]

45
00:05:22,030 --> 00:05:23,448
- [phone ringing]
- Huh?

46
00:05:26,576 --> 00:05:29,913
Where's that coming from?

47
00:05:31,540 --> 00:05:32,958
What the…

48
00:05:34,084 --> 00:05:35,210
Where is it?

49
00:05:35,710 --> 00:05:37,879
It's around here somewhere.

50
00:05:37,963 --> 00:05:39,673
- [ringing gets louder]
- Ah!

51
00:05:39,756 --> 00:05:40,757
[groans]

52
00:05:42,092 --> 00:05:43,343
JIEUN

53
00:05:43,426 --> 00:05:45,178
- Hey!
<i>- </i>[Jieun] <i>Hey.</i>

54
00:05:45,262 --> 00:05:47,764
<i>The kids want to know when you're coming.</i>

55
00:05:47,848 --> 00:05:49,724
<i>- Here, it's Auntie.</i>
<i>- When are you coming?</i>

56
00:05:49,808 --> 00:05:51,893
<i>Auntie, I miss you.</i>

57
00:05:51,977 --> 00:05:54,354
My cuties! You missed me?

58
00:05:54,437 --> 00:05:55,730
Ugeun, Uyeong!

59
00:05:55,814 --> 00:05:57,941
I'll see you on Sunday.
What should I bring you?

60
00:05:58,024 --> 00:06:00,443
<i>Jisun! You don't need to bring anything.</i>

61
00:06:00,527 --> 00:06:01,695
<i>We're going camping,</i>

62
00:06:01,778 --> 00:06:02,863
<i>- so come hungry…</i>
<i>- </i>Gosh.

63
00:06:02,946 --> 00:06:03,989
<i>…and have some barbecue.</i>

64
00:06:04,072 --> 00:06:06,783
<i>You're already a lifesaver</i>
<i>for watching the kids.</i>

65
00:06:06,867 --> 00:06:08,159
[♪ cheerful music plays]

66
00:06:15,584 --> 00:06:16,918
[car unlocks]

67
00:06:32,976 --> 00:06:35,061
[students chattering]

68
00:06:35,145 --> 00:06:39,399
SANGCHEON HAEON

69
00:06:40,859 --> 00:06:42,235
- [student 1] Hello, Ms. Kang!
- [student 2] You're late!

70
00:06:42,319 --> 00:06:43,820
No, I'm not!

71
00:06:44,863 --> 00:06:45,947
[chuckles]

72
00:06:46,948 --> 00:06:51,703
[teacher] Inside a bubbling volcano,
chemical reactions are taking place.

73
00:06:51,786 --> 00:06:53,955
Once the pressure exceeds its limit…

74
00:06:55,707 --> 00:06:56,958
it erupts.

75
00:06:57,042 --> 00:06:58,460
[students cheering]

76
00:07:05,258 --> 00:07:06,301
[student, in English] Me!

77
00:07:06,384 --> 00:07:08,553
- I know!
- Me!

78
00:07:08,637 --> 00:07:11,348
[in Korean]
That's why we multiply both by two.

79
00:07:11,431 --> 00:07:13,725
The amount of pizza is the same.

80
00:07:13,808 --> 00:07:16,436
We're just dividing it differently.

81
00:07:20,106 --> 00:07:23,234
Hi, I'm Kim Soyeon.
You guys already know that, right?

82
00:07:23,985 --> 00:07:25,153
[chuckles]

83
00:07:25,779 --> 00:07:29,741
Number one.
I got into an idol training academy

84
00:07:29,824 --> 00:07:32,619
with 200 applicants
competing for one spot.

85
00:07:32,702 --> 00:07:35,830
[students exclaiming] For real?

86
00:07:35,914 --> 00:07:39,876
Number two.
These days, I only eat one meal a day.

87
00:07:39,959 --> 00:07:41,753
[clamoring]

88
00:07:43,004 --> 00:07:44,005
Number three.

89
00:07:44,089 --> 00:07:46,549
My MBTI type is ESTP.

90
00:07:46,633 --> 00:07:48,551
[students chattering]

91
00:07:48,635 --> 00:07:49,969
GUESS YOUR CLASSMATES' TTL

92
00:07:50,053 --> 00:07:52,389
[Jisun] Soyeon seems pretty sure
what she wants to be, right?

93
00:07:52,472 --> 00:07:53,473
[students] Yes!

94
00:07:54,432 --> 00:07:55,767
Which one is a lie?

95
00:07:56,434 --> 00:07:58,687
The lie is…

96
00:07:58,770 --> 00:08:01,064
- number two.
- [Jisun] Number two.

97
00:08:01,147 --> 00:08:02,273
[Jisun chuckles]

98
00:08:02,899 --> 00:08:03,983
All right, next.

99
00:08:08,822 --> 00:08:10,615
I'm Min Hyunsoo.

100
00:08:12,117 --> 00:08:13,326
Number one.

101
00:08:13,827 --> 00:08:15,954
I like science and art.

102
00:08:16,037 --> 00:08:17,372
[students murmuring]

103
00:08:17,455 --> 00:08:18,456
Number two.

104
00:08:19,499 --> 00:08:21,751
I transferred to Sangcheon in third grade.

105
00:08:21,835 --> 00:08:23,294
[clamoring]

106
00:08:25,755 --> 00:08:26,756
Number three.

107
00:08:27,924 --> 00:08:32,345
My mom always said I was a good boy
whenever I ate broccoli.

108
00:08:32,429 --> 00:08:34,806
[students chattering]

109
00:08:34,889 --> 00:08:35,974
Mmm…

110
00:08:36,057 --> 00:08:38,309
Which of the three is the lie?

111
00:08:38,393 --> 00:08:40,687
Idiot, you got it wrong.

112
00:08:41,521 --> 00:08:44,107
[Jisun] Whether you're right or wrong,
you make your own choice.

113
00:08:45,859 --> 00:08:47,444
He was in my class last year.

114
00:08:47,527 --> 00:08:49,279
That dork doesn't eat broccoli.

115
00:08:50,321 --> 00:08:51,781
Number one is the lie.

116
00:08:51,865 --> 00:08:53,533
- What?
- Nice.

117
00:08:53,616 --> 00:08:55,785
- Okay, we'll stop with Hyunsoo.
- [bell chiming]

118
00:08:57,037 --> 00:08:59,831
You got to know a lot more
about each other, right?

119
00:08:59,914 --> 00:09:01,416
[students] Yes!

120
00:09:01,499 --> 00:09:03,043
[Jisun] Thanks for introducing yourselves.

121
00:09:03,126 --> 00:09:05,295
- Let's have a great year together.
- [students] Okay.

122
00:09:05,378 --> 00:09:06,921
[Jisun] A round of applause for everyone.

123
00:09:14,554 --> 00:09:16,139
- [exclaims]
- Man, you're such a loser.

124
00:09:16,222 --> 00:09:17,307
- So embarrassing.
- [student] Hey!

125
00:09:17,390 --> 00:09:19,225
You still eat what your mom tells you to?

126
00:09:19,309 --> 00:09:20,894
- Mama's boy!
- Stop it.

127
00:09:20,977 --> 00:09:22,145
Min Hyunsoo!

128
00:09:23,354 --> 00:09:25,273
Come here.
Looks like you forgot something.

129
00:09:26,983 --> 00:09:28,526
[bully] Why now? Seriously.

130
00:09:28,610 --> 00:09:30,236
[student 2] Hey, cut him some slack.

131
00:09:37,327 --> 00:09:40,163
[sighs] You haven't turned in
your reading plan, have you?

132
00:09:41,915 --> 00:09:43,041
I have.

133
00:09:45,418 --> 00:09:48,046
Oh, here it is. My mistake.

134
00:09:48,963 --> 00:09:51,174
You need to get to your next class.
Let's leave together.

135
00:09:59,140 --> 00:10:00,141
What is it?

136
00:10:03,770 --> 00:10:05,772
Did you make me stay behind on purpose?

137
00:10:07,607 --> 00:10:10,068
Because you were worried
they'd pick on me?

138
00:10:14,823 --> 00:10:18,159
The other kids
don't need to know your secret.

139
00:10:23,998 --> 00:10:27,752
You have music for next period, right?
Should I walk you to the music room?

140
00:10:28,711 --> 00:10:29,712
No, it's fine.

141
00:10:39,597 --> 00:10:41,266
[teacher 1] Okay,
let's come up with a plan.

142
00:10:41,349 --> 00:10:42,684
- [teacher 2] Okay.
- [teacher 3] Okay.

143
00:10:42,767 --> 00:10:44,978
- [teacher 1] Ms. Kang, you're here.
- Hello.

144
00:10:45,061 --> 00:10:47,605
[teacher 1] You're making coffee too.
We were just about to have some.

145
00:10:47,689 --> 00:10:49,440
Would you mind making ours too?

146
00:10:49,524 --> 00:10:50,650
[teacher 2] Thanks.

147
00:10:59,534 --> 00:11:01,494
With two pumps of syrup.

148
00:11:01,578 --> 00:11:03,746
- [teacher 1, in English] Thank you.
- [Jisun, in Korean] No problem.

149
00:11:04,372 --> 00:11:06,249
- With three pumps of syrup.
- [teacher 2] Thank you.

150
00:11:06,332 --> 00:11:07,333
Sure.

151
00:11:08,585 --> 00:11:10,170
A hot Americano for you.

152
00:11:10,253 --> 00:11:11,504
- Enjoy.
- Thanks.

153
00:11:11,588 --> 00:11:12,589
Ms. Kang.

154
00:11:16,259 --> 00:11:18,720
The vice principal hasn't
said anything to you, has he?

155
00:11:19,679 --> 00:11:20,930
No, he hasn't.

156
00:11:21,472 --> 00:11:24,058
[teacher] I heard you didn't teach
during reading and writing class.

157
00:11:25,602 --> 00:11:27,520
[chuckles] Oh, that?

158
00:11:27,604 --> 00:11:30,815
It's the start of the semester,
so we did some introductions with a game.

159
00:11:32,233 --> 00:11:34,402
We got a complaint from a parent.

160
00:11:34,485 --> 00:11:36,070
They asked why you did that in class

161
00:11:36,154 --> 00:11:37,906
when they'll get to
know each other anyway.

162
00:11:40,116 --> 00:11:42,452
Well, speaking skills are important.

163
00:11:42,535 --> 00:11:44,913
An integrated approach that
combines reading, writing,

164
00:11:44,996 --> 00:11:47,123
and speaking helps build
a strong foundation for learning.

165
00:11:47,207 --> 00:11:50,001
[chuckles] That's all great and all,

166
00:11:50,084 --> 00:11:52,170
but you need to give them
written feedback too.

167
00:11:52,253 --> 00:11:54,547
That way,
you'll have something to show the parents.

168
00:11:55,548 --> 00:11:57,926
Well, I'm not teaching
just to have something to show.

169
00:12:02,680 --> 00:12:05,642
I understand your approach to teaching,

170
00:12:05,725 --> 00:12:11,231
but wouldn't you need good feedback
from parents to get your contract renewed?

171
00:12:13,524 --> 00:12:14,984
[both chuckle]

172
00:12:15,735 --> 00:12:17,237
You know what I mean, right?

173
00:12:18,905 --> 00:12:20,573
- Yes.
- [teacher chuckles]

174
00:12:21,157 --> 00:12:22,533
- [teacher] Thank you.
- No problem.

175
00:12:25,495 --> 00:12:26,871
- [♪ soft music plays]
- [thud]

176
00:12:26,955 --> 00:12:28,414
Of course I'm pissed off.

177
00:12:28,498 --> 00:12:30,500
They're sticking their noses
into everything.

178
00:12:31,084 --> 00:12:32,085
[acquaintance] It's a private school.

179
00:12:32,168 --> 00:12:33,461
The parents weren't happy.

180
00:12:33,544 --> 00:12:37,173
It's not like they're the ones studying.
Elementary school writing is really hard.

181
00:12:37,257 --> 00:12:39,259
"Why does a country need taxes?"

182
00:12:39,342 --> 00:12:41,386
"Arguments for and against
the death penalty."

183
00:12:41,469 --> 00:12:43,596
"How should we prepare
for the end of humanity?"

184
00:12:43,680 --> 00:12:44,847
You try answering those.

185
00:12:44,931 --> 00:12:47,517
[acquaintance] If you're told not to
do something, just don't do it.

186
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:51,896
This is serious enough to file a complaint
with the Office of Education.

187
00:12:51,980 --> 00:12:52,981
[slurping noodles]

188
00:12:55,149 --> 00:12:56,693
Are you even listening?

189
00:12:56,776 --> 00:12:57,777
Nope.

190
00:12:58,987 --> 00:12:59,988
[exclaims]

191
00:13:00,071 --> 00:13:03,032
How can you sit there slurping noodles
after hearing all that?

192
00:13:03,116 --> 00:13:05,285
Then you should've said it right there.

193
00:13:05,368 --> 00:13:07,620
"Reading is for developing thoughts.

194
00:13:07,704 --> 00:13:09,539
Writing is for putting them into words.

195
00:13:09,622 --> 00:13:12,667
That's why it's important
to express one's thoughts regularly.

196
00:13:12,750 --> 00:13:15,378
Telling me not to do introductions
shows you have no idea.

197
00:13:15,461 --> 00:13:18,840
If you don't know anything,
stop interfering with my teaching!

198
00:13:20,425 --> 00:13:22,343
And make your own coffee from now on!

199
00:13:22,427 --> 00:13:24,554
How long do I have to be
your personal barista,

200
00:13:24,637 --> 00:13:25,930
counting the pumps of syrup?

201
00:13:26,014 --> 00:13:27,307
You said you have diabetes!"

202
00:13:32,520 --> 00:13:33,855
[chopsticks clatter]

203
00:13:33,938 --> 00:13:35,940
[exhales deeply]
Man, that's what I needed.

204
00:13:36,024 --> 00:13:37,025
- Bottoms up.
- Whoa, geez.

205
00:13:37,108 --> 00:13:38,067
I thought you were mad.

206
00:13:38,151 --> 00:13:39,444
- Cheers!
- Cheers.

207
00:13:41,029 --> 00:13:43,656
If you keep biting your tongue
and end up speaking up later,

208
00:13:43,740 --> 00:13:46,659
you think they'll think about
how hard it must have been for you?

209
00:13:46,743 --> 00:13:48,453
Never going to happen.

210
00:13:48,536 --> 00:13:49,912
[Jisun] Okay, that's enough.

211
00:13:49,996 --> 00:13:53,249
Some things have to be said
at a certain point.

212
00:13:53,332 --> 00:13:54,917
If it passes that, it's meaningless.

213
00:13:55,001 --> 00:13:56,044
I said, that's enough.

214
00:13:56,544 --> 00:13:57,795
Geez.

215
00:13:57,879 --> 00:14:01,132
This is exactly why your sister
worries you're going to be single forever.

216
00:14:02,550 --> 00:14:04,427
My sister? She never said that to me.

217
00:14:04,510 --> 00:14:05,511
She said that to you?

218
00:14:06,220 --> 00:14:07,221
No.

219
00:14:07,889 --> 00:14:10,224
I mean, of course she's worried.
She's your sister.

220
00:14:10,308 --> 00:14:13,061
And honestly,
even at your previous school, you…

221
00:14:14,771 --> 00:14:17,482
This is on me,
so would you kindly shut up now?

222
00:14:17,565 --> 00:14:19,484
Yes, ma'am. Thank you for the meal.

223
00:14:22,278 --> 00:14:26,365
SANGCHEON HAEON

224
00:14:34,999 --> 00:14:36,000
[vocalizes]

225
00:14:36,084 --> 00:14:37,335
[teacher] Ms. Kang!

226
00:14:37,418 --> 00:14:39,170
I heard Mr. Ha Sunwoo arrived early.

227
00:14:39,253 --> 00:14:41,672
I think he's at the café,
so hurry over and get him.

228
00:14:41,756 --> 00:14:44,967
But I don't know what he looks like.

229
00:14:46,511 --> 00:14:49,305
Oh, right. He's that author
who never shows his face, isn't he?

230
00:14:50,431 --> 00:14:52,266
Well, I'm sure you'll recognize him.

231
00:14:52,350 --> 00:14:54,143
You're both in the same field after all.

232
00:14:55,603 --> 00:14:57,480
SOMETIMES IT RAINS IN MY HEART

233
00:14:57,563 --> 00:14:59,148
BOOK CONCERT
WITH AUTHOR HA SUNWOO

234
00:15:11,577 --> 00:15:14,580
[♪ intriguing music plays]

235
00:15:18,417 --> 00:15:19,544
[Jisun] Sir?

236
00:15:25,383 --> 00:15:26,843
It's an honor to meet you.

237
00:15:27,468 --> 00:15:29,720
No, the honor is mine.
It's nice to meet you.

238
00:15:30,429 --> 00:15:32,223
[Jisun] Sorry to keep you waiting.
Come with me.

239
00:15:35,601 --> 00:15:36,769
Already?

240
00:15:36,853 --> 00:15:38,896
[Jisun] Yes. Let me show you the way.

241
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:48,573
I really love that line.

242
00:15:49,532 --> 00:15:52,577
"Until the day I can open
the umbrella in my heart,

243
00:15:52,660 --> 00:15:54,871
I decided to just
quietly listen to the rain.

244
00:15:56,164 --> 00:15:57,665
Because once the rain has passed,

245
00:15:57,748 --> 00:16:00,918
flowers will begin to bloom
along the dirt paths in my heart."

246
00:16:03,629 --> 00:16:07,758
That's a passage from
<i>Sometimes It Rains in My Heart</i>.

247
00:16:11,137 --> 00:16:13,306
[chuckles] Right. Yes.

248
00:16:13,389 --> 00:16:14,390
Yes.

249
00:16:18,769 --> 00:16:21,355
"Sometimes it rains in my heart."

250
00:16:35,244 --> 00:16:36,370
Come on in.

251
00:16:38,915 --> 00:16:40,041
Pardon?

252
00:16:40,124 --> 00:16:42,043
Feel free to say whatever you'd like.

253
00:16:44,879 --> 00:16:45,922
Wait, I'm--

254
00:16:46,005 --> 00:16:49,133
[Jisun] Everyone, this is the author
that's joining us today.

255
00:16:49,217 --> 00:16:51,385
Please welcome him
with a big round of applause.

256
00:16:51,469 --> 00:16:52,637
[applause]

257
00:16:52,720 --> 00:16:53,721
[♪ cheerful music plays]

258
00:16:53,804 --> 00:16:55,056
[Jisun] Come on in.

259
00:17:15,201 --> 00:17:16,452
Hello, everyone.

260
00:17:16,535 --> 00:17:18,704
[students] Hello.

261
00:17:33,719 --> 00:17:37,974
Do you know how many times
your heart beats in a minute?

262
00:17:38,057 --> 00:17:40,726
- [student 1] Sixty!
- [student 2] Sixty times!

263
00:17:40,810 --> 00:17:44,814
[Junho] Yes, normally,
it beats 60 to 100 times.

264
00:17:44,897 --> 00:17:46,065
[students exclaim]

265
00:17:46,148 --> 00:17:51,237
Now, has anyone ever put their ear
against someone's left chest

266
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:53,781
and listened to their heartbeat?

267
00:17:53,864 --> 00:17:55,825
- [students] Me!
- [♪ gentle music plays]

268
00:17:55,908 --> 00:17:57,034
What did it sound like?

269
00:17:57,118 --> 00:17:58,869
- [student 1] Pitter-patter.
- Ba-bump.

270
00:17:58,953 --> 00:18:01,163
- [student 2] Thump, thump.
- Thump, thump.

271
00:18:01,247 --> 00:18:02,873
- [student 1] Ba-dump, ba-dump.
- Ba-dump, ba-dump.

272
00:18:04,041 --> 00:18:05,042
Thud, thud.

273
00:18:06,294 --> 00:18:08,421
[footsteps approaching]

274
00:18:12,008 --> 00:18:13,801
Hello, may I help you?

275
00:18:13,884 --> 00:18:16,804
Oh, I'm Ha Sunwoo, the author.

276
00:18:17,513 --> 00:18:21,017
I'm looking for the multipurpose room,
but I can't seem to find it.

277
00:18:21,767 --> 00:18:25,563
I listened to the heartbeat
get fainter and fainter,

278
00:18:25,646 --> 00:18:30,067
and I cried until it was almost morning,
then ended up falling asleep.

279
00:18:30,651 --> 00:18:33,070
When I woke up,
I thought maybe it was all a dream.

280
00:18:33,779 --> 00:18:38,284
But no, the cat was right there
in front of me, looking at me.

281
00:18:38,367 --> 00:18:40,536
- [♪ soft music plays]
- But it was strange.

282
00:18:41,203 --> 00:18:42,872
Even though the cat wasn't next to me,

283
00:18:43,414 --> 00:18:47,335
I could hear its heartbeat again.
Ba-bump, ba-bump.

284
00:18:50,212 --> 00:18:54,216
Everyone's heartbeat sounds different.

285
00:18:55,009 --> 00:19:00,556
And it changes with our emotions too,
just like our voice does.

286
00:19:01,974 --> 00:19:02,975
[inhales sharply]

287
00:19:03,059 --> 00:19:04,185
So tonight…

288
00:19:05,186 --> 00:19:11,150
uh, try listening to your parents'
heartbeat and your pet's too.

289
00:19:11,984 --> 00:19:15,821
Because that rhythm is their story.

290
00:19:22,244 --> 00:19:23,245
[applause]

291
00:19:26,332 --> 00:19:27,750
Ms. Kang!

292
00:19:27,833 --> 00:19:29,335
What's going on?

293
00:19:29,418 --> 00:19:32,296
That's Mr. Ha Sunwoo. He's incredible.

294
00:19:32,838 --> 00:19:35,925
This is Mr. Ha Sunwoo, right here.

295
00:19:40,638 --> 00:19:43,933
- I'm sorry. I'm really sorry.
- [Sunwoo] Hello, my fellow book lovers.

296
00:19:44,016 --> 00:19:45,851
I'm Ha Sunwoo, the author.

297
00:19:45,935 --> 00:19:47,687
- [students] Hello.
- I'm sorry.

298
00:19:47,770 --> 00:19:50,398
[teacher] What an embarrassing blunder.

299
00:19:51,023 --> 00:19:53,943
My apologies. I'm so sorry.

300
00:19:54,902 --> 00:19:57,279
[chuckles softly] Don't worry about it.

301
00:19:57,363 --> 00:20:02,034
Thanks to her, I had a chance
to talk to the kids about the heart.

302
00:20:02,118 --> 00:20:06,205
[teacher chuckles awkwardly]
She's still pretty new here,

303
00:20:06,288 --> 00:20:09,208
so she didn't quite know the ropes
and made a mistake like this.

304
00:20:09,875 --> 00:20:12,128
I'd really appreciate your understanding.

305
00:20:12,211 --> 00:20:13,462
It's all right.

306
00:20:13,546 --> 00:20:14,755
[phone buzzes]

307
00:20:14,839 --> 00:20:16,048
Sorry. One moment.

308
00:20:17,717 --> 00:20:19,927
Yes, ma'am. Are you on your way?

309
00:20:21,262 --> 00:20:22,263
[sighs]

310
00:20:26,517 --> 00:20:31,313
I'd like to open an umbrella
in your heart too.

311
00:20:33,065 --> 00:20:34,275
Ah… [chuckles]

312
00:20:36,360 --> 00:20:37,611
But who are you?

313
00:20:39,488 --> 00:20:41,866
I'm here for the parent meeting.

314
00:20:45,494 --> 00:20:47,079
What do you do for a living?

315
00:20:48,581 --> 00:20:50,249
I'm a cardiovascular surgeon.

316
00:20:51,584 --> 00:20:52,585
Ah…

317
00:20:52,668 --> 00:20:54,211
- [teacher] Yes, thank you.
- That explains it.

318
00:20:54,295 --> 00:20:56,964
- [teacher] Sir, this way, please.
- [Junho] Yes.

319
00:20:58,549 --> 00:20:59,633
[Jisun] I'm sorry.

320
00:21:05,222 --> 00:21:06,432
[sighs]

321
00:21:12,188 --> 00:21:13,606
[♪ stirring music plays]

322
00:21:29,455 --> 00:21:31,207
[parent 1] No matter how hard we try,

323
00:21:31,290 --> 00:21:34,251
we can't compete with the infrastructure
in advanced countries overseas.

324
00:21:34,335 --> 00:21:36,378
That's why I'm asking you
to establish direct exchange

325
00:21:36,462 --> 00:21:39,799
and cooperation agreements with schools
in English-speaking countries.

326
00:21:39,882 --> 00:21:44,428
Exactly. It definitely makes
a difference with the school's support.

327
00:21:44,512 --> 00:21:47,181
Yes, I understand that you mean

328
00:21:47,264 --> 00:21:50,935
we should work toward creating
a more enriching educational environment

329
00:21:51,018 --> 00:21:53,270
through a variety of exchanges.

330
00:21:53,354 --> 00:21:55,189
That's not what we meant.

331
00:21:57,233 --> 00:21:58,359
What did you mean, then?

332
00:22:00,361 --> 00:22:01,529
Mr. Min.

333
00:22:02,780 --> 00:22:05,282
- Yes?
- Please share your thoughts.

334
00:22:10,955 --> 00:22:14,875
Most of you here
have taken your kids abroad

335
00:22:14,959 --> 00:22:18,587
for short-term language programs
during the school break, right?

336
00:22:18,671 --> 00:22:22,424
But you're short on information
about which places are best,

337
00:22:22,508 --> 00:22:26,595
and then you have to deal with logistics
like accommodations and airport pickups.

338
00:22:26,679 --> 00:22:27,888
- That's right.
- Yes.

339
00:22:27,972 --> 00:22:33,727
So you usually book through an agency,
but since they require payment up-front…

340
00:22:33,811 --> 00:22:36,355
- [principal] Thank you.
- [parents] Thank you.

341
00:22:36,438 --> 00:22:38,816
- See you next time.
- [parent 1] Yes, see you soon.

342
00:22:41,151 --> 00:22:45,239
[parent 2 gasps] Hey, he's such a catch.

343
00:22:45,322 --> 00:22:47,658
- You said his wife passed away?
- [parent 1] That's what I heard.

344
00:22:47,741 --> 00:22:50,077
He's a real catch
that's back on the market.

345
00:22:53,831 --> 00:22:55,457
- [student] Ms. Kang?
- [Jisun] Yes?

346
00:22:57,084 --> 00:22:59,503
Why don't you ever teach us anything?

347
00:22:59,587 --> 00:23:00,671
IF I HAD A SUPERPOWER?

348
00:23:03,090 --> 00:23:06,927
Like Mr. Ha Sunwoo said earlier,
studying is important,

349
00:23:07,970 --> 00:23:10,139
but it's even more important
to grow as a person.

350
00:23:11,181 --> 00:23:12,558
Why do we need to study?

351
00:23:16,228 --> 00:23:19,148
Well, so we can make lots of money.

352
00:23:19,231 --> 00:23:20,733
Money is important too,

353
00:23:21,275 --> 00:23:24,904
but what's even more important
is knowing yourself.

354
00:23:28,490 --> 00:23:29,491
[student] Yes, ma'am.

355
00:23:30,618 --> 00:23:32,995
[Jisun] "If I had a superpower."

356
00:23:34,455 --> 00:23:36,081
Having a superpower doesn't mean

357
00:23:36,790 --> 00:23:38,959
you have to use it
to get whatever you want

358
00:23:39,043 --> 00:23:41,670
or save the world like some superheroes.

359
00:23:43,130 --> 00:23:44,381
For example…

360
00:23:46,300 --> 00:23:48,260
you could see someone you miss.

361
00:23:49,511 --> 00:23:51,931
Or you could meet someone
who's no longer in this world

362
00:23:52,014 --> 00:23:53,766
and ask them questions.

363
00:23:53,849 --> 00:23:54,850
[♪ soft music plays]

364
00:23:55,643 --> 00:23:57,728
Who would you like to meet most?

365
00:23:59,939 --> 00:24:03,025
Why don't you picture that person
in your mind?

366
00:24:15,371 --> 00:24:16,580
[sobs]

367
00:24:22,294 --> 00:24:25,047
Anyone who opens their eyes
has to clean the library.

368
00:24:29,885 --> 00:24:32,513
Thank you so much for coming today.
I know you're busy.

369
00:24:33,013 --> 00:24:34,723
[Junho] Not at all. I'm a parent too.

370
00:24:35,599 --> 00:24:37,184
You should join the board.

371
00:24:37,267 --> 00:24:40,729
Our sons are in the same class,
so it'd be good to join hands.

372
00:24:40,813 --> 00:24:42,815
I'd like that too.

373
00:24:42,898 --> 00:24:45,651
But I'd end up missing meetings
because of emergency surgeries.

374
00:24:45,734 --> 00:24:47,778
That's a pretty good excuse, isn't it?

375
00:24:47,861 --> 00:24:49,279
[chuckles]

376
00:24:49,363 --> 00:24:52,282
Gosh, I can't argue
with that one. [chuckles]

377
00:24:52,825 --> 00:24:54,493
You'll stay to watch the class, right?

378
00:24:54,576 --> 00:24:56,161
Yes, I'll watch for a bit.

379
00:24:57,663 --> 00:24:59,873
There's no such thing
as a good or bad emotion.

380
00:25:01,000 --> 00:25:05,379
If you keep holding in negative emotions
like sadness or anger,

381
00:25:06,171 --> 00:25:08,632
they'll grow inside you
without you even realizing it.

382
00:25:08,716 --> 00:25:11,343
And eventually,
those emotions will start controlling you.

383
00:25:11,969 --> 00:25:16,890
But if you give names
to those emotions that you want to hide

384
00:25:16,974 --> 00:25:17,975
and get to know them…

385
00:25:18,726 --> 00:25:20,936
- [♪ peaceful music plays]
- …then you'll understand what they are.

386
00:25:22,229 --> 00:25:23,564
And you'll feel a lot better.

387
00:25:26,066 --> 00:25:27,276
You're doing great.

388
00:25:29,737 --> 00:25:31,780
The emotion exercise we did today

389
00:25:31,864 --> 00:25:33,699
is about getting to know yourself better

390
00:25:33,782 --> 00:25:35,868
and becoming more comfortable
with who you are.

391
00:25:58,974 --> 00:26:03,353
KANG JISUN, READING AND WRITING

392
00:26:08,901 --> 00:26:11,195
I WILL HELP MY STUDENTS
FIND THEIR WAY THROUGH BOOKS

393
00:26:22,247 --> 00:26:23,791
[phone buzzes]

394
00:26:27,628 --> 00:26:28,629
Hello?

395
00:26:32,007 --> 00:26:33,217
Police?

396
00:26:39,181 --> 00:26:41,100
CYBERCRIME INVESTIGATION UNIT

397
00:26:41,183 --> 00:26:42,351
[Jisun] Hello.

398
00:26:44,728 --> 00:26:45,771
Hyunsoo.

399
00:26:46,772 --> 00:26:48,190
[investigator] Oh…

400
00:26:48,273 --> 00:26:50,025
Are you Ms. Kang Jisun, his teacher?

401
00:26:50,109 --> 00:26:52,361
Yes, what's going on?

402
00:26:52,444 --> 00:26:54,071
You're his homeroom teacher, right?

403
00:26:56,115 --> 00:26:57,699
Well, I am one of his teachers.

404
00:26:59,034 --> 00:27:00,077
[investigator] Hey.

405
00:27:00,160 --> 00:27:01,870
You said she was your homeroom teacher.

406
00:27:05,374 --> 00:27:07,918
I'm his homeroom teacher,
who teaches one of the subjects.

407
00:27:10,796 --> 00:27:13,715
[investigator] He bought a pair of
counterfeit designer sneakers

408
00:27:13,799 --> 00:27:16,426
and sold them online,
passing them off as authentic.

409
00:27:17,219 --> 00:27:18,804
And they're women's sneakers,

410
00:27:19,471 --> 00:27:21,932
so he clearly didn't buy them for himself.

411
00:27:22,015 --> 00:27:24,226
He intended to sell them from the start.

412
00:27:25,185 --> 00:27:27,354
This is what we call a premeditated crime.

413
00:27:28,355 --> 00:27:29,356
I'm sorry.

414
00:27:30,065 --> 00:27:31,733
[investigator]
You have nothing to apologize for.

415
00:27:34,111 --> 00:27:35,988
What's going to happen to Hyunsoo now?

416
00:27:36,071 --> 00:27:38,448
He'll get a protective disposition
because of his age,

417
00:27:38,532 --> 00:27:40,284
but he could be sent
to juvenile detention.

418
00:27:41,577 --> 00:27:42,703
- [computer mouse clicks]
- [printer whirs]

419
00:27:42,786 --> 00:27:43,787
Just a moment.

420
00:27:47,708 --> 00:27:49,001
Here.

421
00:27:49,084 --> 00:27:51,962
This is the form confirming his release
into a guardian's custody.

422
00:27:52,045 --> 00:27:53,422
Read it and sign there.

423
00:27:54,423 --> 00:27:57,301
He's still so young,
and there must be some misunderstanding.

424
00:27:57,384 --> 00:27:58,594
Hyunsoo wouldn't do that.

425
00:27:58,677 --> 00:28:00,512
Based on our investigation, he would.

426
00:28:01,430 --> 00:28:03,640
Hey, you said you have a father.

427
00:28:04,141 --> 00:28:05,434
You're not going to call him?

428
00:28:05,517 --> 00:28:06,977
My dad's in surgery.

429
00:28:08,562 --> 00:28:10,314
[investigator] You little punk.

430
00:28:10,397 --> 00:28:12,900
Your father's getting surgery,
and you're busy scamming--

431
00:28:12,983 --> 00:28:14,359
He's performing surgery.

432
00:28:15,485 --> 00:28:16,486
[investigator] What?

433
00:28:17,821 --> 00:28:20,032
He's not getting surgery.
He's performing it.

434
00:28:21,575 --> 00:28:22,576
[investigator] He's a doctor?

435
00:28:23,493 --> 00:28:25,454
- [Hyunsoo] Yes.
- I'll meet with the victim

436
00:28:25,537 --> 00:28:27,122
and work things out.

437
00:28:27,205 --> 00:28:29,082
Please give me the victim's phone number.

438
00:28:34,963 --> 00:28:36,048
I'm sorry.

439
00:28:40,844 --> 00:28:42,471
When will your dad be done with surgery?

440
00:28:45,766 --> 00:28:46,892
I don't know.

441
00:28:48,185 --> 00:28:50,479
You didn't call him, did you?
Because he'd get mad?

442
00:28:52,439 --> 00:28:53,565
That's right.

443
00:28:54,775 --> 00:28:56,568
You thought I wouldn't get mad at you?

444
00:29:00,155 --> 00:29:01,782
Did you think I was a pushover?

445
00:29:08,622 --> 00:29:09,873
Have you had dinner?

446
00:29:15,504 --> 00:29:17,673
I won't tell your homeroom teacher.

447
00:29:18,507 --> 00:29:20,550
But you need to tell your dad yourself.

448
00:29:25,013 --> 00:29:26,640
Did you already know?

449
00:29:27,349 --> 00:29:28,350
[Jisun] Know what?

450
00:29:31,603 --> 00:29:33,021
That my mom is not around.

451
00:29:37,776 --> 00:29:38,777
[sighs]

452
00:29:39,444 --> 00:29:41,863
I found out when we played
Two Truths and a Lie.

453
00:29:44,199 --> 00:29:45,200
How?

454
00:29:46,743 --> 00:29:48,912
[Hyunsoo, in flashback]
I like science and art.

455
00:29:49,913 --> 00:29:50,914
Number three.

456
00:29:50,998 --> 00:29:53,792
My mom always said I was a good boy…

457
00:29:53,875 --> 00:29:56,211
[Jisun] "…said I was a good boy
whenever I ate broccoli."

458
00:29:57,295 --> 00:29:59,131
That was the only one in the past tense.

459
00:30:10,100 --> 00:30:12,185
[Hyunsoo] I lied to the other kids…

460
00:30:14,479 --> 00:30:15,981
and pretended I had a mom.

461
00:30:21,194 --> 00:30:22,529
We're kind of alike.

462
00:30:23,238 --> 00:30:24,740
I've done something like that too.

463
00:30:30,954 --> 00:30:34,791
[clicks tongue] My parents passed away
when I was in high school.

464
00:30:36,001 --> 00:30:40,380
One day, I lied to a friend from my club
and pretended my parents were still alive.

465
00:30:41,256 --> 00:30:43,550
Little did I know,
that friend thought I was weird.

466
00:30:45,052 --> 00:30:48,597
Later, I found out
the whole school already knew about it.

467
00:30:50,932 --> 00:30:54,061
Ever since that day,
I don't talk about my parents to anyone.

468
00:31:01,276 --> 00:31:05,655
The other kids
don't need to know your secret.

469
00:31:07,783 --> 00:31:08,784
Bingo.

470
00:31:08,867 --> 00:31:11,578
Then is it okay for me to keep lying?

471
00:31:11,661 --> 00:31:12,829
[chuckles]

472
00:31:18,752 --> 00:31:21,213
[♪ relaxing music plays]

473
00:31:21,296 --> 00:31:25,133
School Library
TEACHER KANG JISUN

474
00:31:39,815 --> 00:31:42,651
[Junho] I knocked,
but I guess you didn't hear it.

475
00:31:43,610 --> 00:31:45,654
A-Are you…

476
00:31:46,822 --> 00:31:49,533
[chuckles] Yes, the fake author.

477
00:31:51,034 --> 00:31:52,077
[chuckles]

478
00:31:53,203 --> 00:31:54,830
But what brings you here?

479
00:31:57,332 --> 00:31:59,584
I'm Hyunsoo's dad.

480
00:32:10,053 --> 00:32:11,221
It's not easy.

481
00:32:13,473 --> 00:32:15,058
After Hyunsoo's mom left us,

482
00:32:16,518 --> 00:32:19,020
I tried to do my best raising him
on my own, but…

483
00:32:21,815 --> 00:32:23,483
He said he needed money.

484
00:32:24,609 --> 00:32:27,863
Apparently, I brag too much
every time I give him his allowance,

485
00:32:28,697 --> 00:32:30,907
- so he wanted to try making his own money.
- [chuckles]

486
00:32:32,909 --> 00:32:36,580
Come to think of it,
I guess I did brag a little.

487
00:32:36,663 --> 00:32:37,914
[chuckles]

488
00:32:39,708 --> 00:32:43,128
You don't have to blame yourself too much.

489
00:32:43,211 --> 00:32:45,088
I guess he's unhappy with everything I do.

490
00:32:46,506 --> 00:32:49,050
He tells me not to use his birthday
as the door code,

491
00:32:49,843 --> 00:32:52,220
not to make him breakfast without asking…

492
00:32:53,346 --> 00:32:54,472
He's my son,

493
00:32:55,307 --> 00:32:57,475
but I really don't know
what goes on in his head.

494
00:33:00,270 --> 00:33:04,608
I wish he'd tell me how he feels,
but he just doesn't.

495
00:33:07,652 --> 00:33:11,948
Expressing your thoughts
isn't as easy as you might think.

496
00:33:14,534 --> 00:33:16,620
And yet, that's what you teach them to do.

497
00:33:18,038 --> 00:33:20,040
Then I guess
I haven't taught him very well.

498
00:33:20,123 --> 00:33:21,583
[chuckles]

499
00:33:24,211 --> 00:33:26,004
[smacks lips, inhales deeply]

500
00:33:26,588 --> 00:33:28,048
This is nice. [chuckles]

501
00:33:28,757 --> 00:33:32,510
To be honest, I've never had anyone
I could complain about my son to.

502
00:33:33,511 --> 00:33:34,638
[chuckles]

503
00:33:37,724 --> 00:33:40,352
I know Hyunsoo has put you through a lot,

504
00:33:40,435 --> 00:33:42,812
and I'd rather take you to dinner
than just coffee.

505
00:33:42,896 --> 00:33:44,481
When are you free?

506
00:33:46,775 --> 00:33:47,901
Oh…

507
00:33:49,486 --> 00:33:52,113
That's very kind of you, but…

508
00:33:53,031 --> 00:33:56,910
we shouldn't meet with parents
outside of school.

509
00:33:56,993 --> 00:33:58,078
[♪ quiet music plays]

510
00:33:58,870 --> 00:33:59,871
Ah… [chuckles]

511
00:33:59,955 --> 00:34:00,956
Right.

512
00:34:04,084 --> 00:34:07,045
Then would it be okay
after Hyunsoo graduates?

513
00:34:10,340 --> 00:34:11,591
I guess so?

514
00:34:11,675 --> 00:34:14,052
There's an early
graduation track here, right?

515
00:34:14,135 --> 00:34:15,845
[chuckles]

516
00:34:22,060 --> 00:34:23,937
[Junho inhales deeply]

517
00:34:25,063 --> 00:34:26,356
It's getting dark out.

518
00:34:26,439 --> 00:34:27,816
Oh, I'll turn on the lights.

519
00:34:27,899 --> 00:34:29,693
No, I should get going.

520
00:34:31,027 --> 00:34:32,028
[rummaging]

521
00:34:34,281 --> 00:34:38,326
These are candies
an ENT doctor I know swears by.

522
00:34:38,410 --> 00:34:40,912
They're good for your throat,
and they're not too sweet.

523
00:34:42,372 --> 00:34:43,373
Thank you.

524
00:34:45,583 --> 00:34:46,584
Sure.

525
00:34:46,668 --> 00:34:47,711
Goodbye then.

526
00:34:59,472 --> 00:35:00,473
If…

527
00:35:03,602 --> 00:35:05,395
If we ever happen to run into each other,

528
00:35:06,146 --> 00:35:08,106
let's grab a coffee then.

529
00:35:27,042 --> 00:35:29,044
- [♪ cheerful music plays]
- [children laughing, chattering]

530
00:35:33,632 --> 00:35:35,592
- I'm here!
- Hey!

531
00:35:35,675 --> 00:35:38,428
- Ugeun, Uyeong, Auntie's here!
- You got here so fast.

532
00:35:38,511 --> 00:35:41,306
[laughs] How have you been? My babies!

533
00:35:44,392 --> 00:35:45,644
[sighs]

534
00:35:46,645 --> 00:35:48,688
- They're fast asleep.
- Hmm?

535
00:35:51,566 --> 00:35:53,151
[chuckles] They passed out.

536
00:35:53,234 --> 00:35:55,612
Are they okay sleeping like that?
[chuckles]

537
00:36:02,786 --> 00:36:04,871
Do you know Dr. Min Junho?

538
00:36:04,954 --> 00:36:06,414
He works at your hospital, right?

539
00:36:06,498 --> 00:36:09,834
Yeah, he's the star of our hospital.

540
00:36:11,378 --> 00:36:12,629
Why?

541
00:36:12,712 --> 00:36:16,216
Oh, I met him once to talk about his son.

542
00:36:16,299 --> 00:36:18,927
Wait. Are you interested in him?

543
00:36:20,595 --> 00:36:21,680
[Jieun] He has a kid.

544
00:36:22,389 --> 00:36:23,431
He's single, though.

545
00:36:25,058 --> 00:36:26,059
Yeah, he is.

546
00:36:31,356 --> 00:36:32,524
So?

547
00:36:34,901 --> 00:36:36,569
I'm just saying.

548
00:36:37,737 --> 00:36:40,073
So, what did you think of him?

549
00:36:41,491 --> 00:36:43,076
What do you mean? [chuckles]

550
00:36:43,952 --> 00:36:45,036
I don't know.

551
00:36:45,704 --> 00:36:47,664
He just seemed like a pretty decent guy.

552
00:36:48,957 --> 00:36:51,626
Oh. What did you two talk about?

553
00:36:51,710 --> 00:36:53,461
We talked about his son, obviously.

554
00:36:54,754 --> 00:36:55,755
But…

555
00:36:57,006 --> 00:37:00,510
he said he wanted to treat me to dinner
to thank me for something.

556
00:37:01,386 --> 00:37:03,888
Wait, he asked you out on a date.

557
00:37:05,140 --> 00:37:07,392
Is that what he meant?

558
00:37:07,475 --> 00:37:08,977
[parent] Yeah.

559
00:37:09,060 --> 00:37:10,895
[Jieun] So what did you say?

560
00:37:10,979 --> 00:37:13,398
I said no. He's a student's parent.

561
00:37:13,481 --> 00:37:15,400
- Well done.
- [Jieun] What?

562
00:37:15,483 --> 00:37:17,402
What's wrong with having dinner with him?

563
00:37:17,485 --> 00:37:19,028
[parent] His kid is her student.

564
00:37:19,112 --> 00:37:21,406
[Jieun] Well,
you don't know about him, honey.

565
00:37:21,489 --> 00:37:23,450
Dr. Min Junho…

566
00:37:23,533 --> 00:37:25,869
I mean, anyone would say he's a catch.

567
00:37:25,952 --> 00:37:28,872
Plenty of people at our hospital
have their eye on him.

568
00:37:28,955 --> 00:37:29,956
[parent] Come on.

569
00:37:30,665 --> 00:37:32,459
That still doesn't make it okay.

570
00:37:38,214 --> 00:37:40,049
How's Junghyeon doing?

571
00:37:41,301 --> 00:37:42,385
[both chuckle]

572
00:37:42,469 --> 00:37:44,429
I liked that guy.

573
00:37:45,096 --> 00:37:48,600
I heard he even got a job at the hospital.
I'm telling you, it's because of you.

574
00:37:48,683 --> 00:37:49,809
[Jisun sighs]

575
00:37:49,893 --> 00:37:52,353
He's in the General Affairs Department?

576
00:37:52,437 --> 00:37:53,521
Patient Services.

577
00:37:54,481 --> 00:37:55,982
[parent chuckles] Yeah, anyway…

578
00:37:56,065 --> 00:37:58,359
I heard you two used to date.

579
00:37:58,443 --> 00:38:00,987
You ever think about
getting back together?

580
00:38:01,070 --> 00:38:02,113
Nope, never.

581
00:38:03,531 --> 00:38:04,991
[heaves]

582
00:38:22,926 --> 00:38:24,135
[♪ stirring music plays]

583
00:39:12,809 --> 00:39:15,436
This is my usual walking route.

584
00:39:19,315 --> 00:39:21,693
I didn't expect to run into you like this.

585
00:39:35,498 --> 00:39:37,083
I see you've got two.

586
00:39:40,503 --> 00:39:43,256
Just in case I happen to run into you…

587
00:39:46,092 --> 00:39:47,260
[♪ pensive music plays]

588
00:39:47,969 --> 00:39:49,137
[chuckles softly]

589
00:40:08,323 --> 00:40:11,701
Let's have dinner instead of coffee.

590
00:40:15,413 --> 00:40:18,416
It's morning, so let's start with coffee.

591
00:40:18,499 --> 00:40:20,043
[both chuckle]

592
00:40:20,835 --> 00:40:22,045
[♪ cheerful music plays]

593
00:40:27,342 --> 00:40:28,384
[in English] Too much.

594
00:40:30,345 --> 00:40:31,763
[in Korean] Nope.

595
00:40:33,056 --> 00:40:35,725
Oh, man. Why do I have nothing to wear?

596
00:40:35,808 --> 00:40:37,143
Gosh, seriously…

597
00:40:59,082 --> 00:41:00,375
Beautiful day, isn't it?

598
00:41:01,417 --> 00:41:02,961
Going on a date?

599
00:41:03,044 --> 00:41:04,837
Oh, yes.

600
00:41:06,673 --> 00:41:09,634
About thirty years ago,
I had some business to take care of,

601
00:41:09,717 --> 00:41:12,261
so I parked in front of a hospital
for just a minute.

602
00:41:12,345 --> 00:41:13,805
And wouldn't you know it,

603
00:41:13,888 --> 00:41:16,641
this woman from parking enforcement
wrote me a ticket.

604
00:41:17,892 --> 00:41:20,436
I was so mad I rushed over
to give her a piece of my mind,

605
00:41:20,520 --> 00:41:23,147
but she just stared right at me
with this look on her face

606
00:41:23,773 --> 00:41:25,483
like she was a Supreme Court justice.

607
00:41:26,109 --> 00:41:27,402
You know the type, right?

608
00:41:27,485 --> 00:41:29,862
[chuckles] Yeah, I know the type.

609
00:41:30,989 --> 00:41:33,783
We've been married for 30 years,
and she's still like that.

610
00:41:34,951 --> 00:41:37,829
We got married exactly two months
after she gave me that ticket. [laughs]

611
00:41:41,082 --> 00:41:42,208
[♪ tender music plays]

612
00:41:43,710 --> 00:41:46,629
You never know
what's around the corner in life.

613
00:41:47,505 --> 00:41:50,466
There's no point in expecting too much
or being scared of anything.

614
00:41:50,550 --> 00:41:51,592
[chuckles]

615
00:42:12,822 --> 00:42:13,823
[♪ soft music plays]

616
00:42:22,081 --> 00:42:23,249
Oh.

617
00:42:26,210 --> 00:42:28,087
- Hello.
- Hello.

618
00:42:31,090 --> 00:42:32,091
- Please.
- Yes.

619
00:42:38,056 --> 00:42:39,057
[♪ ambient music plays]

620
00:42:42,101 --> 00:42:43,352
[both chuckle]

621
00:42:47,023 --> 00:42:49,942
You look very pretty today.

622
00:42:51,736 --> 00:42:52,820
[chuckles]

623
00:42:54,197 --> 00:42:55,364
Right.

624
00:42:55,448 --> 00:42:56,449
[rustling]

625
00:43:06,167 --> 00:43:07,627
- [Jisun chuckles] Thank you.
- [Junho chuckles]

626
00:43:09,337 --> 00:43:11,130
What kind of flowers are these?

627
00:43:11,214 --> 00:43:13,633
Oh, they're gladiolus.

628
00:43:14,300 --> 00:43:15,384
"Gladiolus"?

629
00:43:16,135 --> 00:43:17,136
Yes.

630
00:43:17,220 --> 00:43:19,180
- They're beautiful.
- [Junho exclaims softly]

631
00:43:20,848 --> 00:43:21,849
Oh, okay.

632
00:43:32,944 --> 00:43:34,403
Should we order some wine?

633
00:43:34,487 --> 00:43:35,488
- Sure.
- All right.

634
00:43:45,915 --> 00:43:47,416
[server] Yes, sir.

635
00:43:49,001 --> 00:43:52,839
The Castello di Monsanto
Chianti Classico, please.

636
00:43:58,553 --> 00:44:00,680
You seem to know a lot about wine.

637
00:44:02,557 --> 00:44:03,558
Oh.

638
00:44:04,684 --> 00:44:06,602
I actually don't.

639
00:44:07,728 --> 00:44:09,313
Here's a tip.

640
00:44:09,397 --> 00:44:12,775
If you order the one
with the longest name on the menu,

641
00:44:13,442 --> 00:44:15,862
you can at least sound like
you know what you're doing.

642
00:44:17,113 --> 00:44:18,447
[both chuckle]

643
00:44:23,536 --> 00:44:27,165
I booked out the whole restaurant tonight.

644
00:44:28,374 --> 00:44:29,834
Oh… [chuckles]

645
00:44:45,474 --> 00:44:47,143
They're extras.

646
00:44:47,226 --> 00:44:51,731
I thought you might feel a little awkward
if the place were completely empty.

647
00:44:53,149 --> 00:44:54,317
[chuckles]

648
00:44:55,943 --> 00:44:58,696
Those two over at that table
look like a real couple.

649
00:45:02,325 --> 00:45:04,285
I should pay them a little extra.

650
00:45:04,368 --> 00:45:05,369
[chuckles]

651
00:45:05,995 --> 00:45:07,413
[♪ stirring music plays]

652
00:45:41,197 --> 00:45:42,198
[rain pattering]

653
00:45:45,660 --> 00:45:46,661
[groans softly]

654
00:45:57,672 --> 00:45:58,673
[groans softly]

655
00:46:01,342 --> 00:46:02,343
[moans]

656
00:46:05,096 --> 00:46:06,138
[groans softly]

657
00:46:07,306 --> 00:46:09,058
- Hello.
- Hello.

658
00:46:09,141 --> 00:46:10,268
- Dr. Min.
- [Junho] Yes?

659
00:46:10,351 --> 00:46:12,937
- Here's your surgery schedule for today.
- Ah.

660
00:46:14,397 --> 00:46:15,398
[inhales sharply]

661
00:46:15,481 --> 00:46:16,565
[sighs]

662
00:46:32,540 --> 00:46:33,874
[♪ unsettling music plays]

663
00:46:34,792 --> 00:46:35,793
[groans softly]

664
00:46:37,545 --> 00:46:38,546
[groaning]

665
00:46:41,465 --> 00:46:42,466
[gags]

666
00:46:48,306 --> 00:46:50,516
- [thud]
- [phone buzzes]

667
00:46:50,599 --> 00:46:51,934
[Junho] <i>Did you sleep well?</i>

668
00:46:52,018 --> 00:46:55,730
<i>Thanks for inviting me in last night.</i>

669
00:46:55,813 --> 00:46:58,482
- [patient] Do you have a girlfriend now?
- Huh?

670
00:46:58,566 --> 00:46:59,859
Am I right?

671
00:47:01,193 --> 00:47:03,237
- What?
- How far have you gotten?

672
00:47:03,821 --> 00:47:05,197
[mimics kissing sound]

673
00:47:05,281 --> 00:47:06,574
Have you kissed?

674
00:47:08,409 --> 00:47:11,662
Yunji, that's crossing the line.

675
00:47:11,746 --> 00:47:14,707
I don't want to go around
talking about someone I like.

676
00:47:21,630 --> 00:47:22,631
[crying]

677
00:47:30,556 --> 00:47:32,850
[Yunji] You can't give a woman
a chance to lose interest.

678
00:47:33,726 --> 00:47:34,769
Huh?

679
00:47:34,852 --> 00:47:36,896
You need a follow-up date.

680
00:47:36,979 --> 00:47:40,066
A date isn't complete
until you ask her out again.

681
00:47:40,149 --> 00:47:42,193
[scoffs] A follow-up date?

682
00:47:44,612 --> 00:47:47,281
But what if I'm coming on too strong?

683
00:47:48,282 --> 00:47:49,283
[sighs]

684
00:47:49,784 --> 00:47:53,245
I texted her, but she hasn't replied.

685
00:47:53,329 --> 00:47:54,372
[phone buzzing]

686
00:48:00,544 --> 00:48:01,545
[phone buzzing]

687
00:48:04,548 --> 00:48:05,549
[sobbing]

688
00:48:09,929 --> 00:48:11,889
INCOMING CALL
MIN JUNHO

689
00:48:13,265 --> 00:48:15,226
[sobbing continues]

690
00:48:15,309 --> 00:48:16,310
[phone buzzes]

691
00:48:16,394 --> 00:48:18,771
[Junho] <i>You drank quite a bit last night,</i>
<i>didn't you?</i>

692
00:48:18,854 --> 00:48:20,731
<i>I ordered you some porridge.</i>

693
00:48:20,815 --> 00:48:22,400
<i>Eat before you head to work.</i>

694
00:48:47,883 --> 00:48:49,760
[bully] Hey, why isn't Ms. Kang here yet?

695
00:48:49,844 --> 00:48:53,222
- [student 1] Yeah, why isn't she here yet?
- Yeah, where is she?

696
00:48:53,305 --> 00:48:55,057
[bully] Maybe the class schedule changed.

697
00:48:55,141 --> 00:48:56,517
Was there an announcement?

698
00:48:57,143 --> 00:48:59,562
[student 2] Maybe she's just running late.

699
00:48:59,645 --> 00:49:02,815
[bully] Hey, at this point,
she's not late. She's a no-show.

700
00:49:05,151 --> 00:49:06,152
[phone buzzes]

701
00:49:06,235 --> 00:49:09,738
INCOMING CALL
ACADEMIC HEAD

702
00:49:09,822 --> 00:49:10,823
[sobbing]

703
00:49:25,629 --> 00:49:26,630
[breathing heavily]

704
00:49:26,714 --> 00:49:28,424
[♪ tense music plays]

705
00:49:59,580 --> 00:50:01,790
- [♪ uneasy music plays]
- [breathing shakily]

706
00:50:08,047 --> 00:50:11,217
[Jisun] I barely remember anything.
Just bits and pieces…

707
00:50:12,009 --> 00:50:13,177
[Jieun] How much did you drink?

708
00:50:13,928 --> 00:50:15,012
I don't know.

709
00:50:15,763 --> 00:50:18,807
I drank quite a bit because I was nervous,
but it wasn't the alcohol.

710
00:50:20,809 --> 00:50:23,646
We were talking on my couch, and then…

711
00:50:28,651 --> 00:50:29,652
My room…

712
00:50:31,904 --> 00:50:33,739
Did we end up in my bed?

713
00:50:39,578 --> 00:50:41,664
I think I told him to stop.

714
00:50:42,248 --> 00:50:45,042
- [Jieun] You think you did?
- I really didn't want that to happen.

715
00:50:45,125 --> 00:50:47,670
- Did you clearly tell him no?
- Jieun.

716
00:50:49,755 --> 00:50:51,340
I don't know, okay?

717
00:50:52,174 --> 00:50:53,300
I don't know.

718
00:50:54,510 --> 00:50:57,221
I just can't remember!

719
00:51:05,271 --> 00:51:07,147
I've worked with him for a long time,

720
00:51:07,856 --> 00:51:09,900
and I don't think he'd do that
if you said no…

721
00:51:09,984 --> 00:51:12,778
I wish this wasn't real either, but it is.

722
00:51:14,363 --> 00:51:15,948
I know it happened.

723
00:51:22,746 --> 00:51:24,039
I'll talk to Dr. Min.

724
00:51:24,123 --> 00:51:25,958
What are you even going to say to him?

725
00:51:26,041 --> 00:51:27,668
Maybe there was a misunderstanding--

726
00:51:27,751 --> 00:51:29,086
Misunderstanding?

727
00:51:29,920 --> 00:51:32,214
Are you saying I might be mistaken?

728
00:51:32,298 --> 00:51:33,841
You said you both drank a lot.

729
00:51:33,924 --> 00:51:36,760
It wasn't because of the alcohol!
Why don't you believe me?

730
00:51:36,844 --> 00:51:39,388
[panting]

731
00:51:39,471 --> 00:51:42,224
I didn't want to sleep with him
on our first date.

732
00:51:43,934 --> 00:51:45,686
Especially not with a student's parent.

733
00:51:48,147 --> 00:51:50,232
And don't meet with him.
He gives me the creeps.

734
00:51:52,359 --> 00:51:54,445
He even had porridge
delivered to my place,

735
00:51:54,528 --> 00:51:55,654
as if he cares about me.

736
00:51:58,490 --> 00:51:59,491
So what are you going to do?

737
00:52:00,451 --> 00:52:02,161
Jisun.

738
00:52:02,244 --> 00:52:03,245
I'm going to report him.

739
00:52:03,329 --> 00:52:05,581
It could make things even harder for you.

740
00:52:11,420 --> 00:52:12,546
I know.

741
00:52:14,423 --> 00:52:16,300
But you know what Junghyeon said to me?

742
00:52:17,718 --> 00:52:20,137
He said some things have to be said
at a certain point.

743
00:52:21,680 --> 00:52:24,224
That if I keep biting my tongue
and finally speak up,

744
00:52:24,308 --> 00:52:26,310
somehow it all becomes my fault.

745
00:52:33,442 --> 00:52:34,860
Don't stop me this time.

746
00:52:55,047 --> 00:52:57,007
MONDAY

747
00:52:57,091 --> 00:52:58,425
[phone buzzes]

748
00:53:02,888 --> 00:53:03,889
[sighs]

749
00:53:05,516 --> 00:53:07,518
Seriously? Calling me on my day off?

750
00:53:08,060 --> 00:53:10,938
[team leader] <i>I need you to come in.</i>
<i>We've got a sexual assault case.</i>

751
00:53:13,023 --> 00:53:15,109
NORTHERN GANGWON
SUNFLOWER CENTER

752
00:53:15,192 --> 00:53:17,069
EXAMINATION AND WAITING ROOM

753
00:53:17,152 --> 00:53:19,113
STANDING TOGETHER

754
00:53:20,239 --> 00:53:21,240
[clattering]

755
00:53:22,991 --> 00:53:23,992
[rustling]

756
00:53:33,293 --> 00:53:36,338
[nurse] You can put your clothes
and underwear in here separately,

757
00:53:36,422 --> 00:53:38,632
and then change into this.

758
00:53:40,092 --> 00:53:43,220
You can take your time.
Just let me know if you need any help.

759
00:53:44,221 --> 00:53:45,222
Okay.

760
00:53:46,223 --> 00:53:48,267
STEP 3
OUTER CLOTHING COLLECTION

761
00:53:48,350 --> 00:53:52,354
STEP 5 - PERPETRATOR STAIN
AND SALIVA SAMPLES

762
00:53:52,438 --> 00:53:54,356
STEP 6
PERPETRATOR PUBIC HAIR SAMPLE

763
00:54:18,797 --> 00:54:22,468
WHAT TO DO AFTER AN ASSAULT

764
00:54:22,551 --> 00:54:25,721
COUNSELING SUPPORT

765
00:54:27,264 --> 00:54:28,265
[door opens]

766
00:54:48,285 --> 00:54:49,620
[♪ unsettling music plays]

767
00:54:50,579 --> 00:54:54,500
Once I tell the police everything,
I don't want to talk about it ever again.

768
00:55:01,924 --> 00:55:02,925
Okay.

769
00:55:04,384 --> 00:55:07,721
Once we get through today,
it'll all be over.

770
00:55:14,353 --> 00:55:17,397
It's atrial fibrillation
of unknown cause, but…

771
00:55:17,481 --> 00:55:18,899
Tell me in layman's terms.

772
00:55:19,608 --> 00:55:20,609
It's an arrhythmia.

773
00:55:21,318 --> 00:55:22,819
Why don't you know what caused it?

774
00:55:23,737 --> 00:55:24,738
[sighs]

775
00:55:24,821 --> 00:55:28,575
When the doctor is talking,
just shut up and listen.

776
00:55:29,451 --> 00:55:32,120
Well, it's nothing too serious
or anything, right?

777
00:55:32,204 --> 00:55:35,415
This kind of thing
is pretty common in elderly people.

778
00:55:35,499 --> 00:55:39,795
Your mother probably had a racing heart
and trouble breathing recently, right?

779
00:55:39,878 --> 00:55:42,005
I don't see her often enough to know.

780
00:55:42,673 --> 00:55:44,591
I'm too busy getting
dragged into court all the time.

781
00:55:44,675 --> 00:55:47,761
[sighs] Try to visit her more often, okay?

782
00:55:49,680 --> 00:55:54,059
She doesn't need surgery yet.
I'll prescribe her some medication.

783
00:55:55,394 --> 00:55:57,229
- [knocking]
- Come in.

784
00:55:58,522 --> 00:56:01,191
There's someone here
from the police station.

785
00:56:02,067 --> 00:56:03,318
Excuse me.

786
00:56:04,945 --> 00:56:06,238
Mr. Min Junho?

787
00:56:06,321 --> 00:56:07,322
[door closes]

788
00:56:08,490 --> 00:56:09,533
How can I help you?

789
00:56:09,616 --> 00:56:12,244
You're under emergency arrest
on suspicion of sexual assault.

790
00:56:12,327 --> 00:56:14,830
You have the right to an attorney
and to remain silent.

791
00:56:14,913 --> 00:56:18,500
You may also challenge
the legality of your arrest.

792
00:56:20,085 --> 00:56:21,253
M-Me?

793
00:56:22,170 --> 00:56:24,089
But who would I…

794
00:56:24,673 --> 00:56:26,425
- [detective] We can talk at the station.
- One moment.

795
00:56:27,551 --> 00:56:28,927
I'm an attorney.

796
00:56:29,720 --> 00:56:31,513
- Has he hired you?
- [attorney] He's going to.

797
00:56:31,597 --> 00:56:33,098
Now tell us what's going on.

798
00:56:33,181 --> 00:56:35,100
File the proper paperwork,
then you can ask.

799
00:56:37,894 --> 00:56:38,979
Shall we?

800
00:56:40,272 --> 00:56:42,024
I'm not done with my patients yet.

801
00:56:42,774 --> 00:56:45,527
I don't know what this is about,
but I'll go after I'm done.

802
00:56:46,320 --> 00:56:47,696
We could handcuff you.

803
00:56:47,779 --> 00:56:49,740
He's a doctor here and has a young son.

804
00:56:49,823 --> 00:56:52,034
Is an emergency arrest really necessary?

805
00:56:52,117 --> 00:56:54,536
- That's for the police to decide.
- [detective 2] Let's go.

806
00:56:55,704 --> 00:56:57,289
Does it look like I'm fleeing?

807
00:56:57,914 --> 00:57:00,917
[scoffs] Sexual assault?

808
00:57:02,669 --> 00:57:04,379
Who reported me?

809
00:57:04,463 --> 00:57:05,464
[people murmuring]

810
00:57:25,859 --> 00:57:26,860
Oh, my gosh.

811
00:57:53,387 --> 00:57:54,513
[♪ uneasy music plays]

812
00:58:08,235 --> 00:58:10,028
[detective] Name, Min Junho.

813
00:58:11,863 --> 00:58:13,115
Is that him?

814
00:58:26,878 --> 00:58:30,006
- [Jisun] <i>Wait…</i>
<i>- </i>[Junho laughs]

815
00:58:31,800 --> 00:58:32,801
[Jisun exclaims]

816
00:58:38,640 --> 00:58:41,435
- Is this it?
- I can get you an umbrella from upstairs.

817
00:58:42,352 --> 00:58:43,395
[laughs]

818
00:58:43,979 --> 00:58:44,980
Why are you laughing?

819
00:58:47,399 --> 00:58:50,610
I was just thinking about
when we first met,

820
00:58:50,694 --> 00:58:55,407
when I said I'd like to open
an umbrella in your heart.

821
00:58:57,617 --> 00:58:58,785
That book…

822
00:59:00,245 --> 00:59:03,081
[in unison]
<i>Sometimes It Rains in My Heart</i>.

823
00:59:06,793 --> 00:59:10,088
But I don't think an umbrella
would do much good in weather like this.

824
00:59:11,923 --> 00:59:14,050
Don't worry about me.
You should go inside.

825
00:59:14,134 --> 00:59:15,135
[Jisun stammers]

826
00:59:15,218 --> 00:59:17,262
You'd probably be better off
calling a cab.

827
00:59:19,181 --> 00:59:20,474
You think so?

828
00:59:22,851 --> 00:59:24,936
Oh. My battery's down to two percent.

829
00:59:27,314 --> 00:59:29,649
I think I'd better just run home.

830
00:59:29,733 --> 00:59:31,067
Oh…

831
00:59:31,151 --> 00:59:33,403
I had a really nice time tonight.

832
00:59:33,487 --> 00:59:34,988
I'll text you when I get home.

833
00:59:35,071 --> 00:59:36,072
Good night.

834
00:59:41,536 --> 00:59:43,163
Dr. Min!

835
00:59:46,082 --> 00:59:47,459
[♪ inquisitive music plays]

836
00:59:50,587 --> 00:59:53,590
She invited me in,
offering to call me a cab.

837
00:59:54,758 --> 00:59:56,551
- Come on in.
- [Junho] Oh, thank you.

838
00:59:58,261 --> 01:00:00,430
- Yes.
- Excuse me.

839
01:00:16,696 --> 01:00:18,740
- Please, have a seat…
- I should probably sit--

840
01:00:20,826 --> 01:00:22,619
- I should, right?
- [Jisun] Yes.

841
01:00:49,145 --> 01:00:51,106
- [phone chimes]
- [Jisun] I got one.

842
01:00:51,189 --> 01:00:52,607
Forty minutes?

843
01:00:55,402 --> 01:00:57,863
Then maybe I should just run home.

844
01:00:57,946 --> 01:01:00,240
It's already on its way.

845
01:01:21,219 --> 01:01:22,262
How about some coffee?

846
01:01:24,764 --> 01:01:25,765
I'm good.

847
01:01:26,308 --> 01:01:28,935
I can't sleep if I drink coffee at night.

848
01:01:45,076 --> 01:01:46,912
How about a glass of wine?

849
01:01:48,288 --> 01:01:49,539
Would you like one?

850
01:01:53,001 --> 01:01:54,002
I mean…

851
01:01:54,669 --> 01:01:56,630
I love that it's nice and awkward, but…

852
01:02:01,343 --> 01:02:03,011
Sure, wine sounds nice.

853
01:02:04,429 --> 01:02:05,430
All right.

854
01:02:09,726 --> 01:02:10,852
[♪ uneasy music plays]

855
01:02:11,645 --> 01:02:14,272
[Junho] <i>We were drinking wine</i>
<i>and listening to music.</i>

856
01:02:17,651 --> 01:02:18,652
Then the mood…

857
01:02:23,949 --> 01:02:26,952
We naturally ended up kissing.

858
01:02:27,035 --> 01:02:28,036
[keyboard clacking]

859
01:02:29,245 --> 01:02:31,122
Who initiated it?

860
01:02:31,206 --> 01:02:32,958
Obviously, he did.

861
01:02:34,000 --> 01:02:36,795
Ms. Kang kissed me first. I'm sure of it.

862
01:02:38,505 --> 01:02:41,007
I remember being
a little surprised myself.

863
01:02:44,970 --> 01:02:46,137
[♪ soulful ambient music plays]

864
01:02:48,098 --> 01:02:50,517
- [rain pattering]
- Looks like it's going to keep raining.

865
01:03:07,575 --> 01:03:08,576
[music stops]

866
01:03:19,921 --> 01:03:21,131
Did you know…

867
01:03:22,507 --> 01:03:23,717
this would happen?

868
01:03:24,759 --> 01:03:26,052
[♪ tentative music plays]

869
01:03:54,914 --> 01:03:56,416
From the moment I first saw you…

870
01:04:00,628 --> 01:04:01,629
I knew.

871
01:04:22,984 --> 01:04:26,905
THE PERFECT LIE

872
01:04:52,806 --> 01:04:55,183
[Jisun sobbing] <i>I don't remember.</i>

873
01:04:56,226 --> 01:04:58,812
My feelings were genuine.
It makes no sense.

874
01:04:58,895 --> 01:05:00,563
I told him to stop. I really…

875
01:05:01,523 --> 01:05:04,067
<i>I swear, it wasn't a situation</i>
<i>where she'd feel uncomfortable.</i>

876
01:05:05,443 --> 01:05:08,029
One of you is clearly lying.

877
01:05:08,113 --> 01:05:09,656
I haven't lied about anything.

878
01:05:09,739 --> 01:05:12,450
I couldn't move. I'm not lying!

879
01:05:14,869 --> 01:05:16,287
<i>That day…</i>

880
01:05:17,997 --> 01:05:19,332
Why did you meet with me?

881
01:05:25,922 --> 01:05:27,257
[♪ unsettling music plays]

882
01:05:36,224 --> 01:05:37,851
THE PERFECT LIE

883
01:05:37,934 --> 01:05:39,853
Translated by Liya Hyunjoo Choi
